values ('e4f5a6b7-8c9d-4f44-9a34-5b6c7d8e9f44', 'victimology', 'Victimology', 'Victimology examines the experience, measurement, causes, consequences, rights, and social response to criminal victimization in the United States. The course covers victimization data, theories, trauma and recovery, victims'' rights, compensation and restitution, advocacy and case management, intimate partner violence, sexual violence, child and youth victimization, elder abuse, disability, human trafficking, hate crime, community and mass violence, restorative justice, secondary victimization, equity, cultural humility, vicarious trauma, and victim-service evaluation.');

