 evidence-aware, and survivor-centered response. Students learn reporting choices, forensic systems, and institutional harms.", "children": [{"id": "c5bf0d43-3204-4c30-afb8-f2503e7b0a2b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sexual Violence Dynamics", "children": [{"id": "4a0f702c-523f-4b95-b666-e7d43fd6a2d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent and coercion"}, {"id": "44d3081c-f34c-445d-b007-1841964522d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Acquaintance assault"}, {"id": "fce584d7-a7db-494e-b5a9-4cdda97ee23e", "type": "concept", "title": "Rape myths"}], "description": "Students learn prevalence, myths, consent, and offender/victim relationship patterns."}, {"id": "cf79444e-1533-4e5c-9043-0a76f917da96", "type": "subtopic", "title": "SANE/SART Response", "children": [{"id": "03c23290-b216-4082-bc2d-17925c3bd0c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Forensic exams"}, {"id": "6f539f92-e413-4463-b34e-a5331847348f", "type": "concept", "title": "Medical advocacy"}, {"id": "73aa7cca-9c29-4c96-81e9-a5890f6f9c04", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence and autonomy"}], "description": "The point is to understand multidisciplinary response."}, {"id": "403ff644-d601-4101-a468-3beb69a62468", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutional and Secondary Harm", "children": [{"id": "10690d2a-d1e9-4916-944e-899eef2f28d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Campus processes"}, {"id": "a63cfe95-f918-4082-a58b-373cfc177281", "type": "concept", "title": "Military context"}, {"id": "a4ece800-befd-43d0-a857-7c562315df70", "type": "concept", "title": "Victim credibility and backlash"}], "description": "Students analyze how systems can retraumatize survivors."}]}, {"id": "6560a1ef-5f0c-4f2c-a1a1-e2d2209b6bad", "type": "topic", "title": "Child Maltreatment, Youth Victimization, ACEs, and Juvenile Justice Intersections", "description": "Children and youth experience victimization in developmentally distinct ways. Students learn maltreatment, ACEs, mandated reporting, and youth justice intersections.", "children": [{"id": 